title: The March on Munich
subtitle: Bavaria's generals use the putsch.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_kapp = 1 and crisis_time = 1 and bavaria_soviet = 2 and bavaria_1920_fate = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 4

= The March on Munich

While Berlin strikes, General von Möhl and Georg Escherich's civil guards declare that they will take no more orders from a government that has fled. The Epp Freikorps and twenty thousand civil guards march on Munich from Ingolstadt and Augsburg.

[? if bav_settled = 1 : The talks with Berlin had half disarmed the Red Army. ?][? if bav_settled = 0 : The Red Army mans the bridges over the Lech and the Isar. ?] The Executive Council asks for everything the party has.

- @relief: Send armed columns from Thuringia and Saxony.
- @rail: Stop the trains behind Epp's lines.
- @surrender: Negotiate a surrender and get the cadres out.

@relief
subtitle: Our militias elsewhere will be thinner for it.
choose-if: red_guards_strength >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: We have no armed columns to send.
on-arrival: {!
Q.bav_strength += 2;
Q.red_guards_strength -= 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}
go-to: fate

@rail
subtitle: The Bavarian railwaymen are ours in Munich and nowhere else.
on-arrival: bav_strength += 1; lean_luxemburgist += 1
go-to: fate

@surrender
subtitle: Munich falls. Fewer of ours will die.
on-arrival: bav_strength = -10; bav_surrendered = 1; lean_unionist += 1
go-to: fate

@fate
title: Munich
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
var score = Q.bav_strength + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4) + (Q.strike_count >= 5 ? 1 : 0);
if (score >= 5) {
    Q.bavaria_1920_fate = 2;
    Q.civil_guards_strength -= 60;
    RG.district('bavaria', {loyalty: 10});
    RG.news('Epp\'s march on Munich breaks down', 2);
} else {
    Q.bavaria_1920_fate = 1;
    Q.bavaria_soviet = 1;
    Q.repression += 8;
    RG.district('bavaria', {members: Q.bav_surrendered ? -0.4 : -0.65, loyalty: -10, repression: 20});
    RG.news('Munich falls: Kahr takes power in Bavaria', 3);
    RG.ledger('The Bavarian Council Republic fell in March 1920.', 'e20_bav_fell');
}
!}

[? if bavaria_1920_fate = 2 : For three days there is fighting at Dachau and on the Theresienwiese. Then the trains behind Epp's lines stop, and his civil guards go home to their farms. The council republic has survived again. ?]

[? if bavaria_1920_fate = 1 : Munich falls on 19 March. Gustav von Kahr becomes master of Bavaria, and the civil guards hunt the council members through the working-class districts. ?][? if bavaria_1920_fate = 1 and bav_surrendered = 1 : Most of our leaders are over the Austrian border by then. ?]
